From 9810e8988b719d12b69cb88ff4b66bb554e1d716 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:31:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(update): a checkpoint refusal names its cause; a
 duplicate `gateway run` is not a second gateway

hermes-hub 2026-11-12 13:53-13:56Z: three instant applies exited 1 with only "busy or cannot
acknowledge an idle pause", and the second one drained and restarted the real gateway on the
old code.

- gateway/update_checkpoint.py: every refusal of `checkpoint-for-update` carries a `reason`
  naming the check (no live intent, nonce, cron inventory, admission not held, unpublished
  reservations, async delegations, unpreservable work by kind with chat session keys, loop
  timeout). The hub's refusals were a gateway-hosted chat turn (lane/oneshot) the checkpoint
  does not preserve.
- hermes_cli/update_cmd_posix_pause.py: `_ask_to_drain` keeps that reason and the deferral
  prints it as `[cause: ...]` after the existing "busy or cannot acknowledge an idle pause"
  token (hermes-sync's retry match is unchanged).
- `_discover_bare` skips a `gateway run` PID that is not its home's verified gateway
  (`live_gateway_pid_for_home` names another PID): a duplicate start that exits once it finds
  the home served. The hub inventoried such PIDs (487116 at 13:54, 2807628 at 12:29, 3768639
  at 13:15) next to the unit gateway: the unit gateway ACKed and drained (Kanban workers
  checkpointed), the duplicate refused, and the rollback restarted the unit on the old code
  (owner_restart_lost, reclaim). Unprovable identity keeps the old behaviour.
